 ploads/event/59.1_20260628184330331793.png
DESCRIPTION:Join your friends and neighbors for the summer potluck precinc
 t meeting. We will be discussing our strategy to Get Out the Vote (GOTV). 
 Signs-ups for poll workers and greeters. How best to approach door knockin
 g. Who should attend: All Dems of the precinct and our left-leaning friend
 s. Bringing a chair is suggested. We will have tables.
LOCATION:Lake Louise Picnic Pavilion\, 63 Lakeshore Dr\, Weaverville\, NC\
 , 28787
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/buncombedems/event/980366/
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Democratic Party
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Getting Ready to Vote 2026: Are You Concerned about the Fall Elect
 ions?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T140000
UID:6b1c453e5227151411db6b8d3b880ba2@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/event/Getting%20Ready%20to%20Vote%202026%20Are%20You%20Concerned%20
 about%20the%20Fall%20Elections_20260625213453495644.png
DESCRIPTION:Changes to the election process in North Carolina\, as well as
  the potential complications to the voting process proposed by the Trump a
 dministration\, have produced concerns and uncertainty about our fall elec
 tions on the part of party leaders and the general public. Jake Quinn\, cu
 rrent member of the Buncombe County Board of Elections and its former Chai
 r\, will share his knowledge of the implications of the changes to the Boa
 rd of Elections and voting process here in Buncombe County. He will also
LOCATION:Pisgah Valley Clubhouse\, 6 Rhododendron Way\, Candler\, NC\, 287
 15
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/buncombedems/event/979351/
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Democratic Party
END:VEVENT
